---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import LumosDiagram from '../../components/LumosDiagram.astro';
import ContactCta from '../../components/ContactCta.astro';
const steps = [
  { name: 'Vehicle airflow', detail: 'Could airflow generated by passing vehicles become an input to local lighting? This is the starting question. The available energy depends on traffic and airflow conditions.' },
  { name: 'Wind generation', detail: 'The concept explores vertical-axis wind turbines to convert moving air into rotation and electrical energy. The practical question is how much usable energy this stage could provide.' },
  { name: 'Energy storage', detail: 'Generation and lighting demand do not necessarily happen at the same time. Storage connects those stages; its capacity and losses would need to be evaluated together.' },
  { name: 'Wireless transfer', detail: 'A wireless energy transfer demonstration formed part of the project. Its place in a complete lighting system raises questions about range, efficiency and losses.' },
  { name: 'Illumination', detail: 'The concept pairs fluorescent illumination with automatic light sensing, connecting the lighting response to ambient conditions.' }
];
---
<Layout title="LUMOS — Urban Lighting Concept | Salim Youssef Najim" description="LUMOS is a student engineering concept for decentralized urban lighting, exploring vehicle airflow, wind generation, storage and a wireless transfer demonstration." schema={{ '@type': 'CreativeWork', name: 'LUMOS', description: 'Student engineering concept exploring decentralized urban lighting and sustainable energy.', creator: { '@id': 'https://salimyoussefnajim.com/#person' }, url: 'https://salimyoussefnajim.com/projects/lumos/' }}>
  <section class="page-hero section-pad">
    <p class="eyebrow section-index">Projects / Student engineering</p>
    <h1 class="case-title">LUMOS</h1>
    <div class="case-hero-grid"><h2>Decentralized<br/>urban lighting.</h2><p>I led a team exploring how vehicle airflow, wind generation, energy storage and illumination could connect in a sustainable-energy concept.</p></div>
    <dl class="case-facts">
      <div><dt class="eyebrow">Discipline</dt><dd>Energy & systems</dd></div>
      <div><dt class="eyebrow">My role</dt><dd>Team lead</dd></div>
      <div><dt class="eyebrow">Stage</dt><dd>Student concept</dd></div>
      <div><dt class="eyebrow">Focus</dt><dd>SDG 7 / Clean energy</dd></div>
    </dl>
  </section>
  <nav class="page-subnav section-pad" aria-label="LUMOS sections"><a href="#overview">Overview</a><a href="#system">The system</a><a href="#role">My role</a><a href="#evaluation">Further evaluation</a></nav>
  <section id="overview" class="case-illustration section-pad reveal" aria-labelledby="overview-title">
    <div><p class="eyebrow section-index">01 / Overview</p><h2 id="overview-title">The idea.</h2><p>Could some of the airflow around moving vehicles contribute to a local lighting system? LUMOS develops that question into a connected system concept.</p><p class="note">Concept illustration of the proposed system. Geometry and connections are illustrative.</p></div>
    <LumosDiagram/>
  </section>
  <section id="system" class="case-system section-pad" aria-labelledby="system-title">
    <div class="section-heading reveal"><div><p class="eyebrow section-index">02 / The system</p><h2 id="system-title">Follow the energy.</h2></div><p>Open a stage to see its role in the concept and the questions it raises.</p></div>
    <div class="system-accordion">
      {steps.map((step,i)=><details class="system-step" name="lumos-system" open={i===0}>
        <summary class="system-step-summary"><span class="eyebrow">0{i+1}</span><strong>{step.name}</strong><span class="system-step-indicator" aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary>
        <div class="system-step-body"><p>{step.detail}</p></div>
      </details>)}
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="chapter-section section-pad">
    <div class="reading-intro"><p class="eyebrow section-index">Project notes</p><p>The role, the stage of development and the questions still to be tested.</p></div>
    <div class="chapters">
      <article id="role" class="chapter reveal"><span class="eyebrow">03</span><div><h2>My role.</h2><p>I led the team developing LUMOS, bringing the sustainable-energy idea and its individual elements into a shared project direction.</p></div></article>
      <article class="chapter reveal"><span class="eyebrow">04</span><div><h2>Development stage.</h2><p>LUMOS is a student engineering concept that includes a wireless energy transfer demonstration. Developing it into a complete urban lighting system would require measured performance and reliability testing.</p></div></article>
      <article id="evaluation" class="chapter reveal"><span class="eyebrow">05</span><div><h2>Further evaluation.</h2><ul class="question-list"><li><strong>Energy capture.</strong> How much usable energy could the airflow provide under measured conditions?</li><li><strong>System losses.</strong> How much energy would remain after storage and transfer?</li><li><strong>Practical operation.</strong> What would maintenance, storage and reliability require?</li></ul></div></article>
    </div>
  </section>
  <ContactCta/>
</Layout>
